Problem

Given the head of a linked list, reverse the nodes of the list k at a time.

If the remaining nodes are less than k, leave them as they are.

Optimal Approach :

Approach :

Create temp pointing to head.
Create prevLast to store the last node of the previous reversed group.
Find the kthNode from temp.
If kthNode is NULL, connect the remaining nodes and stop.
Store nextNode = kthNode->next.
Break the list by
kthNode->next = NULL;
Reverse the current group.
If it is the first group,
Update head = kthNode.
Otherwise,
Connect previous group using
prevLast->next = kthNode;
Update
prevLast = temp;
temp = nextNode;
Repeat until the list ends.
Functions Used
1. reverseLinkedList()

Reverses a linked list using the 3-pointer approach.

Returns the new head.

2. getKthNode()

Returns the kth node from the current node.

If less than k nodes are present,

returns NULL.

Time Complexity
O(N)

Every node is visited only once.

Space Complexity
O(1)

Only pointers are used.

Variables to Remember 
Variable	Meaning
temp	First node of current group
kthNode	Last node of current group
nextNode	First node of next group
prevLast	Last node of previous reversed group

Why do we break the list?
kthNode->next = NULL;

Without breaking the list,

reverseLinkedList() would reverse the entire remaining linked list instead of only k nodes.

Why do we store nextNode?
nextNode = kthNode->next;

After breaking the list,

we would lose the remaining nodes.

So we store them before breaking.

Why ???
prevLast = temp;

Before reversing,

temp
 ↓
1 -> 2 -> 3

After reversing,

3 -> 2 -> 1
          ↑
        temp

temp becomes the last node of the reversed group.

We save it because the next reversed group will be connected after it.

Mistakes to Avoid :
Forgetting to check whether k nodes exist.
Forgetting
kthNode->next = NULL;
Forgetting to save
nextNode = kthNode->next;

before breaking the list.

Forgetting
prevLast->next = kthNode;
Forgetting
temp = nextNode;
In getKthNode(), forgetting to decrement k.

Pattern to Remember :

Every iteration follows the same 7 steps:

Find kth node
        ↓
Save nextNode
        ↓
Break the list
        ↓
Reverse
        ↓
Connect previous group
        ↓
Update prevLast
        ↓
Move temp to next group
